.TH MEMO 1 "October 2026" "memo 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
memo \- lightweight Canon Cat inspired text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B memo
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B memo
is a lightweight, zero-dependency, POSIX-compliant full-screen text editor
that implements the modeless editing and LEAP navigation paradigm of the
Canon Cat work processor.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display help summary and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Display version information and exit.
.SH NAVIGATION & EDITING
.TP
\fBRight-ALT (held)\fR
LEAP Forward: increments search string and teleports cursor toward end of buffer.
.TP
\fBLeft-ALT (held)\fR
LEAP Backward: increments search string and teleports cursor toward start of buffer.
.TP
\fBLeft-ALT + Right-ALT\fR
LEAP Both: engages selection span between the leap origin and destination.
.TP
\fBArrow Keys\fR
Local micro-navigation (Up, Down, Left, Right).
.TP
\fBBackspace\fR / \fBDelete\fR
ERASE: deletes character or highlighted span.
.TP
\fBAlt-M\fR
MOVE: relocates highlighted selection to current cursor position.
.TP
\fBAlt-C\fR
COPY: duplicates highlighted selection to current cursor position.
.TP
\fBAlt-U\fR / \fBCtrl-Z\fR
UNDO: reverses last editing transaction.
.TP
\fBCtrl-S\fR
Saves buffer atomically to disk.
.TP
\fBCtrl-Q\fR
Exits memo (prompts if unsaved changes exist).
.SH AUTHORS
memo was created following the design principles of Jef Raskin.
